l\u001b[?1000l\u001b[?1002l\u001b[?1003l\u001b[1;1H\u001b[1;45r\u001b[36;3HThe final whole-branch review hasn't started\u001b[Cyet.\u001b[CI've\u001b[Cmerged\r\n  both roles into the mission\u001b[Cbranch,\u001b[Cand\u001b[Call\u001b[C9\u001b[Ctests\u001b[Cpass.\u001b[CBut\r\n  troupe won't treat the Codex reviewer window as ready, so the  \u001b[39;3Hmessage wasn't sent. It timed out twice, and nothing was typed\u001b[40;3Hinto\u001b[Cthe\u001b[Cwindow.\u001b[41;65H\u001b[1K\r\n  The\u001b[Cwindow\u001b[Cdoes\u001b[Clook\u001b[Cidle\u001b[Cat\u001b[Cits\u001b[Cprompt.\u001b[CIts\u001b[Cstatus\u001b[Cbar\u001b[Cshows\r\n  \"\u26a0\u001b[45;156H\u001b[?25l\u001b[?1006l\u001b[?1000l\u001b[?1002l\u001b[?1003l\u001b[?1006h\u001b[?1000h\u001b[?1002h\u001b[H  troupe won't treat the Codex reviewer window as ready, so the  \u001b[2;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cmessage wasn't sent. It timed out twice, and nothing was typed \u001b[3;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[2G\u001b[1K\u001b[Cinto the window.\u001b[4;65H\u001b[1K\r\n  The window does look idle at its prompt. Its status bar shows  \r\n  \"\u26a0 3 warnings\", which may be what's keeping troupe from seeing \u001b[7;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cit as ready.                                                   \u001b[8;65H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\u001b[2G\u001b[1K\u001b[CTwo ways to unblock it:\u001b[10;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[11;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C1. \u001b[1mClear\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mit\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1myourself:\u001b[m\u000f open the \u001b[38;5;153mreview\u001b[39m window and press \u001b[38;5;153mf2\u001b[39m to   \u001b[12;5H\u001b[1K\u001b[Csee the warnings. Dismiss whatever needs dismissing, then   \u001b[13;5H\u001b[1K\u001b[Ctell me and I'll send the final review.                     \u001b[14;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C2. \u001b[1mLet\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mme\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mrestart\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mthe\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mreviewer:\u001b[m\u000f I close the review window and  \u001b[15;5H\u001b[1K\u001b[Copen a fresh one from the mission branch, which now has both\u001b[16;5H\u001b[1K\u001b[Croles merged. You'd likely have to answer Codex's \"Trust    \u001b[17;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[5G\u001b[1K\u001b[Cthis folder?\" prompt again.\u001b[18;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[19;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[CI'd go with option 1 because it's quicker.                     \u001b[20;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[21;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[COn the page review itself: Codex passed the page branch with no\u001b[22;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cmust-fix findings. It ran the page in a real Chromium browser  \u001b[23;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[2G\u001b[1K\u001b[Cand checked:\u001b[24;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- the theme is set before the page first draws                 \u001b[25;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- the toggle choice survives a reload                          \u001b[26;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- link labels can't inject HTML                                \u001b[27;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- the \"couldn't load links\" fallback appears when it should    \u001b[28;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- nothing scrolls sideways at phone width                      \u001b[29;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[30;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[CIt left one optional suggestion: the page test checks the link \u001b[31;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cdata rather than the finished list on the page, so it wouldn't \u001b[32;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Ccatch someone later swapping in unsafe rendering. The page is  \u001b[33;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Csafe as written. I'll list this as an open finding at the MR   \u001b[34;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cgate rather than spend a fix round on it.                      \u001b[35;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;174m\r\n\u273d\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;216mGusting\u2026\u001b[38;5;174m \u001b[38;5;246m(running\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246mStop\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246mhook\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246m\u00b7\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246m3m\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246m27s\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246m\u00b7\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246m\u2193\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246m2.3k\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246mtokens\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246m\u00b7\u001b[39m         \u001b[37;65H\u00